-- title:
--   Progressive measurability and augmented natural filtrations
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ be a probability space with a filtration $\mathbb F=(\mathcal F_t)_{t\in\mathbb R}$, used on a horizon $[0,T]$.
--
--   1. A process $u$ is **progressively measurable on $[0,T]$** with respect to a family of σ-algebras $(\mathcal G_t)$ if, for every $t\in[0,T]$, $(s,\omega)\mapsto u_s(\omega)$ on $[0,t]\times\Omega$ is $\mathcal B([0,t])\otimes\mathcal G_t$-measurable.
--   2. The **right-continuous augmented natural filtration** of a process $B$ is $\mathcal F^B_t=\bigcap_{s>t}\big(\sigma(B_r:0\le r\le s\wedge T)\vee\mathcal N_P\big)$, where $\mathcal N_P$ is generated by the $P$-null sets.
--
--   These are the stochastic-basis notions used in §§5–7; the usual conditions are the published `RepairSched.UsualConditions` (right-continuous filtration, $\mathcal F_0$ containing every $P$-null set).
--
--   **Formalization Note** Progressive measurability is stated with measurability rather than Mathlib's strong measurability, because flows of sub-probability measures take values in a measurable space without topology.
-- source:
--   Dianetti, Ferrari, Fischer, Nendel, A Unifying Framework for Submodular Mean Field Games, arXiv:2201.07850v1, §5.2 (Def. 5.5 (1), p.20), §6.1 (p.26), §7.1 (p.29)

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory

set_option warn.classDefReducibility false

namespace SubmodMFG.Supplement

/-- **Progressive measurability on `[0, T]`** of a process `u : ℝ → Ω → β` with respect to a
family of σ-algebras `G` (a filtration): for every `t ∈ [0, T]` the map
`[0, t] × Ω → β`, `(s, ω) ↦ u_s(ω)`, is `B([0, t]) ⊗ G_t`-measurable.

**Formalization Note.** Mathlib's `ProgMeasurable` asks for strong measurability into a
topological space; `M≤1`-valued flows (§7) only carry a σ-algebra, so measurability is used.
Values of `u` outside `[0, T]` play no role. -/
def ProgMeasOn {Ω β : Type*} [MeasurableSpace β] (G : ℝ → MeasurableSpace Ω) (T : ℝ)
    (u : ℝ → Ω → β) : Prop :=
  ∀ t ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) T,
    Measurable[@Prod.instMeasurableSpace (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) t) Ω _ (G t)]
      (fun p : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) t × Ω => u p.1 p.2)

/-- The σ-algebra generated by the `P`-null sets (used to augment a natural filtration). -/
def nullSigma {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  MeasurableSpace.generateFrom {A | P A = 0}

/-- The **right-continuous, `P`-augmented natural filtration** of a process `B` on `[0, T]`:
`𝓕^B_t = ⋂_{s > t} (σ(B_r : 0 ≤ r ≤ s ∧ T) ∨ 𝒩_P)`. §7.1, p.29: "denote by F^B the
right-continuous extension of the filtration generated by B, augmented by the P-null sets". -/
def augNatFiltration {Ω β : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] [MeasurableSpace β] (P : Measure Ω)
    (T : ℝ) (B : ℝ → Ω → β) (t : ℝ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨅ s ∈ Set.Ioi t,
    ((⨆ r ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) (min s T), MeasurableSpace.comap (B r) inferInstance) ⊔ nullSigma P)

end SubmodMFG.Supplement


